{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>You know how I have served you.</b> Do not attribute the increase of the flock to the serpent drawn after the constellation, but rather attribute it to the perfection of my service — which was performed with expertise and great diligence in the work of tending the sheep." "<b>And what your livestock was with me.</b> That they had broken bones and illnesses, and I set the broken ones and healed the sick, as is fitting for one who tends cattle."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:35.802945760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}